- Publishing the picked part of the document into the library of the user: one
- button in the head bar, and the link of the library that comes out of it, ready
- for the palette field of another scene.
- @see ../../ARCHITECTURE.md section 5
$bog_vmap_app_publish $mol_view
	store $bog_vmap_app_publish_store
	- Property name of the picked part on the root class, empty when nothing is
	- picked. The button is off without one.
	part \
	- Declaration of the picked part, as the inspector reads it: `Name $base …`.
	source \
	- Method of the part, cut out of the body of the class it belongs to.
	js \
	- Styles of the ROOT CLASS of the document, whole, and not the rule of the
	- part alone: a sub view of the part is a flat property of the root too, so
	- its rule is written beside the rule of the part and nothing in the text says
	- whose it is. Which rules belong to the part follows from the tree the copy is
	- made of, and that tree is built here, so the cut is made here as well.
	css \
	- The root class of the document, as text: the sub-views the editor hoisted
	- out of the part are put back into it from here before it goes out.
	doc \
	- Names of the classes the document authors, root included: a part based on
	- one of them is refused, its base would stay behind.
	classes /string
	- Link of the library land, empty before the first publication.
	lib_link \
	sub <= content /$mol_view
	Publish $mol_button_minor
		title \В библиотеку
		hint <= publish_hint \
		enabled <= enabled false
		click? <=> publish? null
	- The link itself is the caption, so what is copied is what is seen.
	Copy $mol_button_copy
		hint \Скопировать ссылку библиотеки для поля палитры другой сцены
		text <= lib_link
		title <= lib_link
	Note $mol_view
		sub / <= note \
